{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hashgraph-online/hol-guard/pulls/2974","id":4561400866,"node_id":"PR_kwDORzZri88AAAABD-F0Ig","html_url":"https://github.com/hashgraph-online/hol-guard/pull/2974","diff_url":"https://github.com/hashgraph-online/hol-guard/pull/2974.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/hashgraph-online/hol-guard/pull/2974.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hashgraph-online/hol-guard/issues/2974","number":2974,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Fix native lifecycle admission, Windows persistence and risk reuse","user":{"login":"kantorcodes","id":6068672,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNjg2NzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6068672?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kantorcodes","html_url":"https://github.com/kantorcodes","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kantorcodes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kantorcodes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kantorcodes/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kantorcodes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kantorcodes/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kantorcodes/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kantorcodes/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kantorcodes/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kantorcodes/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Native request handling needs to preserve deadlines and authority when resident processes restart, policy generations change or private files are replaced. This PR fixes those boundaries, reuses risk analysis within an unchanged request, and makes validation of all four native wheel targets part of normal CI.\n\nThe current head is [`f8f190a2`](https://github.com/hashgraph-online/hol-guard/commit/f8f190a286159b46bf14a624a62ba52b5d2371a3), targeting `release/3.2`. It adds three conformance test files to `ad9d9238`, with every product and runtime source byte unchanged. The latest source integration adds 53 reviewed source, test, contract and workflow changes on top of `124472b8`. The original [PRD status](https://github.com/hashgraph-online/hol-guard/blob/14e50a701a85890c744be3b17260fd70af3bf831/review-evidence/2026-09-19/pr2974-completion/addenda/20260920T143000Z-integrated-source/PRD-STATUS.md), [TODO](https://github.com/hashgraph-online/hol-guard/blob/14e50a701a85890c744be3b17260fd70af3bf831/review-evidence/2026-09-19/pr2974-completion/addenda/20260920T143000Z-integrated-source/TODO.md) and [Takeaway](https://github.com/hashgraph-online/hol-guard/blob/14e50a701a85890c744be3b17260fd70af3bf831/review-evidence/2026-09-19/pr2974-completion/addenda/20260920T143000Z-integrated-source/TAKEAWAY.md) preserve the original acceptance criteria and remaining qualification work.\n\n**What changes**\n\n- Resident I/O and connection work retain their existing deadline and non-replay guarantees. A publisher can now accept the first generation in a completely observed, empty retained resident directory. Unknown or incomplete scans, changed directory identities, changes to a live generation and post-acknowledgement mutation still refuse readiness.\n- Windows private readers preserve audited descriptor and Unicode CRT behavior. The writer uses extended atomic rename only after positive platform and exact-source-handle capability checks. It selects the original operation before mutation when unavailable, and never retries or falls back after a native attempt.\n- Request-local risk facts are reused only while exact inputs, catalog, authority and implementation bindings remain valid. Approval continuation and effectful callbacks retain their revalidation boundaries; private request context does not become public request state.\n- Native contract documentation distinguishes actual authority, availability, delivery and rollback behavior. Normal CI collects four separate native platform archives, checks pure-wheel equality, and runs the existing strict artifact validator without a Windows waiver. Windows control XML is retained separately, and the new publisher regression is selected on all native build platforms.\n\n**Observed validation**\n\n| Scope | Result | Boundaries |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Final combined Linux source | 108 passed, 17 Windows-only skips; Ruff, formatting and diff checks pass | 125 unique JUnit cases. Full normal source type check: 0 errors and 30,179 warnings across 1,434 files. The only subsequent change adds three workflow selectors; Python source is identical. |\n| Windows 3.10 and 3.12 isolated source | Each 149 passed, 3 POSIX skips | Each includes 53 mandatory Windows cases, 90 child frames, 18 WTEXT pairs and the existing manager atomic replacement selector. |\n| Inactive resident namespace regression | 107 passed, 3 existing Windows-only skips, including 27 new controls | The same two positive regressions fail on unchanged `124472b8` for the intended reasons. The signed publisher control uses an explicit ACK double. |\n| Request risk reuse | Final Python 3.14 lane: 347 passed, no skips, all 13 required positives and 49 approval cases | Earlier supported interpreter/platform results and producer-specific skips remain source-bound in the evidence. Fresh combined matrix runs separately. |\n| Native contract and artifact collector | 118 contract tests; 21 collector/validator controls; one actual old-archive admission | The old four-platform binaries were downloaded and byte-verified. A full six-file release, signing and installed transitions are separate requirements. |\n\nThe [integrated source checkpoint](https://github.com/hashgraph-online/hol-guard/tree/14e50a701a85890c744be3b17260fd70af3bf831/review-evidence/2026-09-19/pr2974-completion/addenda/20260920T143000Z-integrated-source) contains the source publication, original reports, full logs, before/after failures, exact source census and independent technical peers. The [preceding compatibility/artifact checkpoint](https://github.com/hashgraph-online/hol-guard/tree/285b2d951797460c15173a6b3675d725530fdd1c/review-evidence/2026-09-19/pr2974-completion/addenda/20260920T140400Z-compatibility-and-artifacts) preserves the earlier evidence without overwriting failed attempts.\n\n**Current CI and remaining work**\n\nFresh normal CI is running on `f8f190a2`. The prior `ad9d9238` run found four Claude launcher conformance shard failures. The three-file test correction now recognizes only the reviewed Windows reader insertion at its original location, separately pins the reader providers, preserves historical vectors, and rejects repinned or relocated changes. It passes 29 strict binding controls and the affected cohort (74 passed, 29 explicit platform/binary skips); types report 0 errors/87 warnings. Original failed logs remain retained.\n\nThe prior Intel run separately reached `native_policy_not_ready` during its second recovery sample, before native request admission; the underlying policy preparation cause remains unknown. Its Windows source and resident lanes passed, and the installed Windows corpus recorded 21 native decisions and accepted/processed receipts, with a separate unresolved journal permission event retained. Advancing the test fix triggered the workflow's existing concurrency rule and canceled the unfinished prior Linux soak. That run remains incomplete; no prior check or partial soak is credited to the new head. The new head will stay stable while its normal CI completes. Strict release validation requires a coherent four-platform artifact set.\n\nThe Windows controlled error distinction is intentional and documented: original `MoveFileExW` reports WinError 5 and `FileRenameInfoEx` reports 32 for a CRT-held destination. Both retain `PermissionError`/errno 13, one attempt, original contents and cleanup. Native errors are never translated. The former full-code-equality fixture remains a failed historical result; all retained child output bytes are identical in the corrected fixture's successful runs.\n\nOriginal performance and lifecycle qualification is incomplete. The prior installed diagnostic completed 88 calls but all phase joins failed observer admission, and every route ceiling was missed. Its corrected observer passes 76 untimed controls; a new, precisely bound measurement is pending. Ordinary 1,000 ms concurrency smoke does not satisfy the original 200 ms p99 gate, and the 50% long-soak limit does not replace 12% mixed-load RSS. Full matched-host populations, registered routes and source references, mixed receipt/resource load, accepted-change-to-first-decision freshness, signed/frozen artifacts, update/downgrade/rollback and canary evidence remain required.\n\nAll 144 original task objects and 119 catalog entries are retained in the [task overlay](https://github.com/hashgraph-online/hol-guard/blob/14e50a701a85890c744be3b17260fd70af3bf831/review-evidence/2026-09-19/pr2974-completion/addenda/20260920T143000Z-integrated-source/task-status-overlay.json), with original acceptance and dependencies unchanged. Archived statuses are not promoted into current acceptance by this checkpoint. Eligible independent approval of the final head remains a repository gate; technical peers do not substitute for it.\n","created_at":"2026-09-17T17:49:53Z","updated_at":"2026-09-20T15:01:00Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"753850955c33eb15f992d1fe7ca375dd26c3a070","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"deep-purple-boots","id":301892678,"node_id":"U_kgDOEf6ERg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301892678?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deep-purple-boots","html_url":"https://github.com/deep-purple-boots","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deep-purple-boots/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deep-purple-boots/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"ht